Suricata and Zeek (now maintained as Zeek) are open-source network security monitoring (NSM) tools with divergent detection philosophies. Suricata operates as an inline intrusion detection and prevention system (IDPS), utilizing multithreaded signature matching via YARA, Lua, and Emerging Threats (ET) rules. Zeek functions as a passive protocol analyzer, generating detailed connection logs, file extraction, and behavioral analysis.

**Detection of HTTP/2 AitM:**
HTTP/2 abuses like **CVE-2024-21412** (HTTP/2 Rapid Reset DoS) or **CVE-2023-44487** (HTTP/2 Continuation Flood) target load balancers and WAFs. Suricata uses a rule like:
```yaml
alert http2 any any -> any any (msg:"Possible HTTP/2 Continuation Flood";
flow:to_server; http2.continuation.count:>100; threshold:type both, track by_src, count 50, seconds 1;
sid:2035001; rev:1;)
```
Zeek detects anomalies via script `http2-main.zeek`, tracking `orig_h` and `dest_h` for unusual frame sequences:
```zeek
event http2_frame(frame: HTTP2::Frame) {
    if (frame.type == HTTP2::CONTINUATION && |frame.data| > 8192)
        NOTICE([$note=HTTP2_Continuation_Flood,
                $msg=fmt("Possible HTTP/2 flood from %s", frame.orig_h)]);
}
```
